- port this to use different approach: the test setup will generate
  foobar.snap.new,foobar.snap.modified,foobar.snap.deleted temp files in the
  test run. This tool will then work out the updates with the user from those
  files and not work on the streamed test output from `go test -json`. This
  solves the problem below and makese other things easier, by sacrificing some
  intuitivity.
- implement proper message buffering as the go test -json tool will chunk
  outputs and doesnt guarnatee the output order. Different test outputs can
  interleave and longer test inputs basically dont work right now as we
  expected all of the json in a single message. We can probably solve this by
  buffering it by testname into a tx_map and unloading it once we receive the
  end message SNAP@END for a test. This means we need to introduce the message
  via a small protocol. sth like [SNAP@START\n, content messages, SNAP@END\n]
- detect if a snapshot/ input was removed. Ideally with the same ui from the
  incoming data at the end.
